    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here are two true equations based on the information from the table:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Between which two whole numbers is the value of \\(\\log_{10} 600\\)? Be prepared to explain how do you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What do you think logarithm means or does?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Next to “log” is a subscript—a number or letter printed smaller and below the line of text. What do you think the subscript tells us?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What about the other two numbers on either side of the equal sign (for example, the 100 and the 2 in \\(\\log_{10} 100 = 2\\))? What do they tell us?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The term log is short for logarithm. Discuss the following questions with a partner and record your responses:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For which whole number values of \\(n\\) is \\(\\log_{10}(n)\\) an integer?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Why will \\(\\log_{10}(n)\\) never be equal to a non-integer rational number?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We know how to solve equations such as \\(10^a = 10,\\!000\\) or \\(10^b= \\frac{1}{100}\\) by thinking about integer powers of 10. The solutions are \\(a = 4\\) and \\(b = {\\text-}2\\). What about an equation such as \\(10^p = 250\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Because \\(10^2 = 100\\) and \\(10^3 = 1,\\!000\\), we know that \\(p\\) is between 2 and 3. We can use a logarithm to represent the exact solution to this equation and write it as:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle p=\\log_{10} 250\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The expression is read “the log, base 10, of 250.”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The small, slightly lowered “10” refers to the base of 10.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The 250 is the value of the power of 10.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\log_{10} 250\\) is the value of the exponent \\(p\\) that makes \\(10^p\\) equal 250.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Base 10 logarithms are often written without the number 10. So \\(\\log_{10} 250\\) can also be written as \\(\\log 250\\) and this expression is read “the log of 250.”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "One way to estimate logarithms is with a logarithm table. For example, using this base 10 logarithm table we can see that \\(\\log_{10} 250\\) is between 2.3 and 2.48.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L09-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Hello, Logarithm!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The logarithm to base 10 of a number \\(x\\), written \\(\\log_{10}(x)\\), is the exponent you raise 10 to get \\(x\\), so it is the number \\(y\\) that makes the equation \\(10^y = x\\) true. Logarithms to other bases are defined the same way with…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
